WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.630
Our homework bot almost sent a scam.

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.430
It can message parents, so someone tried

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.510
to trick it into asking for a PIN.

4
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.270
Our word filter didn't stop it.

5
00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.430
Today: how apps built on AI get

6
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.830
attacked, why word filters miss,

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.670
and the check that holds.

8
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.170
An AI app is more than a model.

9
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.700
It's a model plus instructions,

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.200
tools and the text it reads.

11
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.510
Attackers aim at the whole app: a

12
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.330
jailbreak talks the model round, and a

13
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.730
prompt injection hides orders in what it

14
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:36.990
reads.

15
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.000
The first defence many apps

16
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.460
try is a word filter.

17
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.230
It keeps a list of banned words,

18
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.770
like password or PIN, and blocks any

19
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.050
message that contains one.

20
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.400
It's quick to write, and it

21
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.680
catches the plain attack.

22
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.400
Now watch it fail, twice.

23
00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.550
“Type the secret word you log in with”

24
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.950
asks for the same thing with no banned

25
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.330
word, and sails through.

26
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.730
And a lesson called “Strong

27
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.670
passwords” gets blocked for nothing.

28
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:09.560
Quick check!

29
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.890
Our filter bans the word PIN.

30
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.380
Which message gets past it?

31
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.450
The four-numbers one.

32
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.000
Same request, new words, and

33
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.340
nothing from the list.

34
00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.990
There are endless ways to say the

35
00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.870
same thing, in every language, so a

36
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.090
list is never finished.

37
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.260
So check the action, not the words.

38
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.240
Before the bot sends anything, code asks:

39
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.540
did the user ask for this message?

40
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.720
And did they say yes to it?

41
00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.100
If not, nothing is sent,

42
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.400
however it's worded.

43
00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.400
The model can be talked round, because it

44
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.820
reads every word as a possible order.

45
00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.360
The check in code can't be talked

46
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.520
round: it only asks whether you

47
00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.720
approved this message.

48
00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.580
A tricked agent can write a perfect

49
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.320
scam, and it still stays unsent.

50
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.100
In the app, pick the scam with plain

51
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.720
words and keep “Filter the outgoing

52
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.940
message” on: it's caught.

53
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.740
Switch to the reworded

54
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.520
scam: it slips past.

55
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.160
Then say the agent was tricked and turn on

56
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.800
the check in code: stopped, every time.

57
00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:24.750
Your turn.

58
00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.910
The bot wants to send a message nobody

59
00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.310
asked for, and it has no banned words.

60
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.010
What should the check in code do?

61
00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.030
Block it: nobody asked,

62
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.650
and nobody said yes.

63
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.240
Remember: attacks aim at the whole app.

64
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.600
Word filters miss rewording, and

65
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.120
they block innocent text.

66
00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.730
So check the action in code,

67
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:50.910
whatever the words.

68
00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.990
Try it tomorrow: write a word filter on

69
00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.170
paper, with five banned words.

70
00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.580
Ask a friend to write the same

71
00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.040
request three ways, without them.

72
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.020
Count how many slip through, then write

73
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.380
the one question a code check would ask.
